From 23329108a92d137e04d51527b1155a54eefc6a2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 09:09:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] sparc64: release IOMMU context on scatterlist mapping
 failure

dma_4u_map_sg() allocates a context before allocating DVMA ranges.
If a range allocation fails, the cleanup releases the mappings but
leaves the context allocated. Repeated failures can exhaust the
context bitmap and force mappings to use the context-0 fallback.

Release the context after unwinding the mappings, while the IOMMU
lock is still held. iommu_free_ctx() already handles context 0.

Fixes: 13fa14e18561 ("[SPARC64]: Add SG merging support back into IOMMU code.")
Reported-by: sashiko-bot <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Magnus Lindholm <linmag7@gmail.com>
---
 arch/sparc/kernel/iommu.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/sparc/kernel/iommu.c b/arch/sparc/kernel/iommu.c
index 7613ab0ffb89..d3c76ee4767f 100644
--- a/arch/sparc/kernel/iommu.c
+++ b/arch/sparc/kernel/iommu.c
@@ -586,6 +586,7 @@ static int dma_4u_map_sg(struct device *dev, struct scatterlist *sglist,
 		if (s == outs)
 			break;
 	}
+	iommu_free_ctx(iommu, ctx);
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&iommu->lock, flags);
 
 	return -EINVAL;
